## Why the Technician Matters at a Wedding

Most of our packages don't include a technician as standard. The Wedding Pack does, alongside only the MICE Pack built for corporate conferences. At a wedding, that matters more than at almost any other event: vows and speeches happen once, live, in front of everyone who matters to you. A technician on site catches a microphone feedback loop or a dropped connection before it becomes the thing people remember, and adjusts sound levels as the day moves from ceremony to speeches to dancing.

## What We Stock, and What We Source

We provide sound, lighting and microphones for the ceremony and reception, plus the technician to run it. The Wedding Pack has no projector, screen or LED display, since a wedding rarely needs one. Furniture, decor and dancefloor accessories are not in our own inventory, and neither are cameras, filming or photography. If a page or vendor implies otherwise, ask them to itemize it: AV equipment and those other trades are typically separate services.

If your wedding still has a gap in one of those areas, tell us what it is. We can pass the request on to our supplier contacts and tell you whether it can be covered on your date. Anything sourced that way is labelled as such on the quote.

